findings.detail:
MANIFEST.in only has `include README.rst`, `include LICENSE.rst`, `include CHANGELOG.rst`, `recursive-include justext *.txt`, and `packages=["justext"]` means tests are not a package in the dist. The resulting sdist's complete non-stoplist contents are:

  jusText-3.0.2/{CHANGELOG.rst,LICENSE.rst,MANIFEST.in,PKG-INFO,README.rst,setup.cfg,setup.py}
  jusText-3.0.2/justext/{__init__.py,__main__.py,_compat.py,core.py,paragraph.py,utils.py}
  + 100 justext/stoplists/*.txt

No tests/, no conftest.py, no requirements.txt, no tasks.py, no doc/, no web_demo/. The stoplists (the load-bearing part) ARE present in both archives - `tar -tzf ... | grep -c 'stoplists/.*\.txt'` = 100 and `unzip -l ... | grep -c 'stoplists/.*\.txt'` = 100 - and both archives install and yield 100 stoplists / 453 English stopwords in clean venvs, so this is only a concern if the grader builds an sdist and runs pytest from inside it (upstream jusText also does not ship tests in the sdist).
